    <h1>Replacing the Meltano taps with faucet-stream</h1>
    <p class="lede">Can faucet-stream drop into <code>DrivetrainAi/meltano_taps</code> — 46 sources into one BigQuery target — and produce the same raw tables? <strong>All framework gaps this analysis identified are now merged to <code>main</code></strong> (#510–#518, #501 via #524/#526; #527/#530/#531 via #532). Re-scored under your rules: <strong>ignore <code>_sdc_</code> columns</strong>, count <strong>inbuilt transforms</strong> and the <strong>SQL transform</strong>, <strong>never count WASM</strong>.</p>
    <p class="meta"><b>Rules applied:</b> _sdc_* dropped · inbuilt transforms count · SQL transform counts (and is flagged) · WASM does not count · <b>sink:</b> faucet-sink-bigquery · <b>goal:</b> in-place replace, same tables · Singer excluded — verdicts use each tap's real transport.<br><b>Shipped since rev 2:</b> composable/session/signing auth (#511) · OData + $metadata discovery (#512) · bookmark→request push-down (#513) · async-job pattern (#514) · response-decode base64/gunzip/unzip/parse csv·xlsx·xml (#515) · unpivot/lookup/json_encode inbuilt transforms (#516) · endpoint discovery (#517) · scoped overwrite (#518) · discovery matrix (#501) · <code>_faucet_*</code> metadata columns (#510).<br><b>Merged since rev 3 (PR #532):</b> in-run datetime window slicing (#527) · inbuilt <code>tree_flatten</code> recursive report-tree → rows (#530) · chained/two-level discovery + collected list dimensions (#531) · staged-load foundation (#528, partial) · persistent run logs (#529). · <b>updated:</b> 2026-08-21</p>
  </header>

  <div class="band">
    <div class="stat ok"><div class="n">40<span class="delta">▲5</span></div><div class="l">Supported</div><div class="d">Stock connector + inbuilt transforms (unpivot / lookup / json_encode / <code>tree_flatten</code>).</div></div>
