150	    <p class="lede">Can faucet-stream drop into the <code>meltano_taps</code> monorepo — 47 sources into one BigQuery target — and produce the same raw tables? <strong>Every framework gap this analysis identified is now merged to <code>main</code></strong> — including the last two (staged bulk load and the <code>cross_join</code> transform) via <strong>PR #537</strong>. Re-scored under your rules: <strong>ignore <code>_sdc_</code> columns</strong>, count <strong>inbuilt transforms</strong> and the <strong>SQL transform</strong>, <strong>never count WASM</strong>.</p>
151	    <p class="meta"><b>Rules applied:</b> _sdc_* dropped · inbuilt transforms count · SQL transform counts (and is flagged) · WASM does not count · <b>sink:</b> faucet-sink-bigquery · <b>goal:</b> in-place replace, same tables · Singer excluded — verdicts use each tap's real transport.<br><b>Shipped since rev 2:</b> composable/session/signing auth (#511) · OData + $metadata discovery (#512) · bookmark→request push-down (#513) · async-job pattern (#514) · response-decode base64/gunzip/unzip/parse csv·xlsx·xml (#515) · unpivot/lookup/json_encode inbuilt transforms (#516) · endpoint discovery (#517) · scoped overwrite (#518) · discovery matrix (#501) · <code>_faucet_*</code> metadata columns (#510).<br><b>Merged in rev 3 (PR #532):</b> in-run datetime window slicing (#527) · inbuilt <code>tree_flatten</code> recursive report-tree → rows (#530) · chained/two-level discovery + collected list dimensions (#531) · staged-load foundation (#528, partial) · persistent run logs (#529).<br><b>Merged in rev 5 (PR #537):</b> inbuilt <code>cross_join</code> transform (#534) — <code>ukg_pro</code> now needs no SQL · ClickHouse + MSSQL staged bulk load (#528, execution) · rest <code>partitions</code> fan-out data-loss fix (#535) · repeated/array query params (#536).<br><b>Merged in rev 8 (PR #545):</b> XML source <code>decode:</code> pipeline (#540) · flow-auth sign-on-login-step (#541) · flow-auth capture from headers/Set-Cookie/XML (#542) · async_job <code>fetch.url_from</code> (#543) · XML body-cursor paging (#544) — the last framework gaps; oracle_fusion / skyslope / acumatica / sage are now config-driven. <b>updated:</b> 2026-08-23</p>
