163	      <h3>✓ Rev 10 — full 47-tap verification against real code (the "200% sure" pass)</h3>
164	      <p><strong>Every tap was re-read from its actual source and checked stream-by-stream against the template.</strong> Primary/core streams are config-driven across all 47. The pass caught <strong>6 real template bugs</strong> (now fixed): <strong>sap</strong> (wrong auth — would never authenticate), <strong>deskera</strong> (same), <strong>ukg_pro</strong> (broken parent-token), <strong>netsuite</strong> (missing header), <strong>ms365bc</strong> (transform order), <strong>ramp</strong> (missing fields).</p>
165	      <p><strong>One systemic bug found — <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/552">#552</a> (tier-1):</strong> a child stream fanned out over multiple parent records into a <code>write_mode: overwrite</code> table is <em>last-writer-wins</em> (each parent truncates the prior) — silent data loss on child-fan-out streams (deel/campfire/dualentry/deskera/bamboohr/navan/ramp-balance-history). Core/single-parent streams are unaffected. Plus per-tap stream-level gaps filed as <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/553">#553</a>–<a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/558">#558</a> (offset-in-body &amp; keyset paging, explode-parent-carry, oauth2 rotation, async locator paging, lookup-from-API) and the shopify ShopifyQL pair (<a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/550">#550</a>). So: <strong>primary-stream config-driven everywhere; specific child/report/incremental streams have named, issue-linked gaps.</strong></p>
166	    </div>
