171	      <h3>✓ Round-5 merged (PR #545): the last framework gaps closed — 44 / 47 config-driven, 3 partial (vendor-only), 0 blocked</h3>
172	      <p>The four taps that building the real templates had exposed as gap-blocked are now fully config-driven, each via a merged enhancement: <strong>oracle_fusion</strong> (base64-XLSX-in-SOAP → the XML source's <code>decode:</code> pipeline, #540), <strong>skyslope</strong> (HMAC-signed login → flow sign-on-login-step, #541), <strong>acumatica</strong> (Set-Cookie session → flow header/cookie capture, #542), and <strong>sage</strong> (XML session capture #542 + <code>readMore</code> body-cursor paging #544). <strong>stripe</strong>'s report-CSV also became config-driven (async_job <code>fetch.url_from</code>, #543); its only remaining gap is the vendor SDK's list model. <strong>No framework gap remains</strong> — the 3 Partials (shopify, stripe, plaid) are all per-connector vendor specifics.</p>
