178	      <h3>✓ Round-4 merged (PR #537): the fleet is now 41 / 46 fully-supported, 0 needs SQL, 0 blocked</h3>
179	      <p>The two remaining follow-ups from rev 3's build backlog both landed. <strong>The inbuilt <code>cross_join</code> transform (#534)</strong> — a cartesian product of sibling record-arrays within one record — moved <strong>ukg_pro</strong> (job × compensation × employment) off the DuckDB SQL path to Supported inbuilt. <strong>No tap now touches the SQL transform at all.</strong></p>
180	      <p><strong>Staged bulk load is complete (#528).</strong> The ClickHouse <code>s3()</code> and MSSQL <code>COPY INTO</code> execution paths shipped alongside the already-native Redshift/Snowflake/BigQuery loads — so every warehouse sink loads from the object store instead of row-by-row. Also in this PR: the <strong>rest <code>partitions</code> fan-out data-loss fix (#535)</strong> — partitioned streams now fan out under <code>faucet run</code>, not just <code>validate</code> — and <strong>repeated/array query params (#536)</strong> for <code>group_by[]</code>-style APIs. Both underpin the matrix fan-out several taps rely on.</p>
