<title>Meltano taps → faucet-stream parity</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<style>
:root{
  --ground:#f6f7f9; --surface:#ffffff; --surface-2:#f0f2f5;
  --ink:#15181e; --muted:#5a626f; --faint:#878f9c;
  --border:#e2e6ec; --border-strong:#cdd3dc;
  --accent:#0f766e; --accent-ink:#0b5c55; --accent-wash:#e5f2f0;
  --ok:#15803d; --ok-wash:#e7f4ea; --ok-line:#57a86e;
  --core:#a86611; --core-wash:#fbf0dd; --core-line:#d19a3e;
  --part:#c2410c; --part-wash:#fbe9de; --part-line:#e08454;
  --block:#b4241f; --block-wash:#fbe5e3; --block-line:#dc7b76;
  --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(20,24,31,.05),0 6px 20px -12px rgba(20,24,31,.18);
  --mono:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,Consolas,"Liberation Mono",monospace;
  --sans:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]){
  --ground:#0d1014; --surface:#151a20; --surface-2:#1b212a;
  --ink:#e8eaef; --muted:#9aa3b1; --faint:#727c8b;
  --border:#252c36; --border-strong:#333c48;
  --accent:#2dd4bf; --accent-ink:#5fe3d2; --accent-wash:#123232;
  --ok:#5cc07d; --ok-wash:#12241a; --ok-line:#2f6b43;
  --core:#e0a94a; --core-wash:#271e10; --core-line:#6d551f;
  --part:#ef8a5a; --part-wash:#291710; --part-line:#7a3f22;
  --block:#f0827c; --block-wash:#2a1412; --block-line:#7a332f;
  --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3),0 10px 30px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.6);
}}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --ground:#0d1014; --surface:#151a20; --surface-2:#1b212a;
  --ink:#e8eaef; --muted:#9aa3b1; --faint:#727c8b;
  --border:#252c36; --border-strong:#333c48;
  --accent:#2dd4bf; --accent-ink:#5fe3d2; --accent-wash:#123232;
  --ok:#5cc07d; --ok-wash:#12241a; --ok-line:#2f6b43;
  --core:#e0a94a; --core-wash:#271e10; --core-line:#6d551f;
  --part:#ef8a5a; --part-wash:#291710; --part-line:#7a3f22;
  --block:#f0827c; --block-wash:#2a1412; --block-line:#7a332f;
  --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3),0 10px 30px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.6);
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
html{-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
body{margin:0;background:var(--ground);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--sans);
  font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
.wrap{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(1.1rem,4vw,3rem) clamp(1rem,4vw,2.2rem) 5rem}
a{color:var(--accent-ink);text-underline-offset:2px}
h1,h2,h3{text-wrap:balance;line-height:1.15;margin:0}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--accent-ink);font-weight:600}
.masthead{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding-bottom:1.8rem;margin-bottom:2.2rem}
h1{font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.6vw,3rem);letter-spacing:-.02em;font-weight:750;margin:.5rem 0 .6rem}
.lede{font-size:clamp(1.02rem,1.7vw,1.22rem);color:var(--muted);max-width:66ch;margin:0}
.meta{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.74rem;color:var(--faint);margin-top:1.1rem;letter-spacing:.02em;line-height:1.7}
.meta b{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}

.band{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:.7rem;margin:2rem 0 1.4rem}
.stat{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;padding:.95rem 1rem;
  box-shadow:var(--shadow);position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.stat::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:4px}
.stat.ok::before{background:var(--ok-line)} .stat.core::before{background:var(--core-line)}
.stat.part::before{background:var(--part-line)} .stat.block::before{background:var(--block-line)}
.stat .n{font-size:2rem;font-weight:750;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1}
.stat .delta{font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;font-family:var(--mono);margin-left:.35rem;vertical-align:middle}
.stat.ok .delta{color:var(--ok)} .stat.block .delta{color:var(--ok)} .stat.core .delta{color:var(--ok)}
.stat .l{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.4rem}
.stat .d{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--faint);margin-top:.3rem;line-height:1.4}

section{margin-top:2.6rem}
h2{font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.4vw,1.6rem);letter-spacing:-.01em;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.3rem}
h2 .num{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;color:var(--accent-ink);font-weight:600;margin-right:.6rem;letter-spacing:.05em}
.sub{color:var(--muted);max-width:74ch;margin:.35rem 0 1.1rem}

.callout{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border-strong);border-radius:14px;
  padding:1.3rem 1.4rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow);border-left:4px solid var(--accent)}
.callout.good{border-left-color:var(--ok-line)}
.callout.note{border-left-color:var(--core-line)}
.callout h3{font-size:1.06rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.callout p{margin:.5rem 0;color:var(--muted)}
.callout p strong{color:var(--ink)}
.callout code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85em;background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;padding:.05rem .32rem}

.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;margin:.6rem 0 0;font-size:.86rem;color:var(--muted)}
.legend b{color:var(--ink)}
.legend .pill{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.68rem;padding:.12rem .5rem;border-radius:20px;margin-right:.3rem;font-weight:600}
.pill.all{color:var(--ok);background:var(--ok-wash);border:1px solid var(--ok-line)}
.pill.core{color:var(--core);background:var(--core-wash);border:1px solid var(--core-line)}

.tablewrap{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);background:var(--surface)}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:940px;font-size:.86rem}
thead th{position:sticky;top:0;background:var(--surface-2);z-index:2;text-align:left;
  font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);
  padding:.7rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-strong);white-space:nowrap}
tbody td{padding:.62rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:top}
tbody tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}
tbody tr{border-left:3px solid transparent}
tr.ok{border-left-color:var(--ok-line)} tr.core{border-left-color:var(--core-line)}
tr.part{border-left-color:var(--part-line)} tr.block{border-left-color:var(--block-line)}
td.src{font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap}
td.src .cat{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.66rem;color:var(--faint);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.02em;margin-top:.1rem}
td.mech{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.76rem;color:var(--muted);min-width:140px}
td.note{color:var(--muted);min-width:300px;line-height:1.45}
td.note em{color:var(--accent-ink);font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.82em}
.v{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.03em;padding:.2rem .5rem;border-radius:20px;white-space:nowrap;display:inline-block}
.v.ok{color:var(--ok);background:var(--ok-wash);border:1px solid var(--ok-line)}
.v.part{color:var(--part);background:var(--part-wash);border:1px solid var(--part-line)}
.v.block{color:var(--block);background:var(--block-wash);border:1px solid var(--block-line)}
.scope{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;padding:.12rem .4rem;border-radius:5px;margin-left:.4rem;white-space:nowrap;text-transform:uppercase}
.scope.all{color:var(--ok);background:var(--ok-wash);border:1px solid var(--ok-line)}
.scope.core{color:var(--core);background:var(--core-wash);border:1px solid var(--core-line)}
.filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.2rem 0 1rem;align-items:center}
.chip{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.74rem;letter-spacing:.03em;border:1px solid var(--border-strong);
  background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);border-radius:20px;padding:.34rem .8rem;cursor:pointer;
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;transition:background .15s,color .15s,border-color .15s}
.chip .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%}
.chip[data-k=all] .dot{background:var(--ok-line)} .chip[data-k=core] .dot{background:var(--core-line)}
.chip[data-k=part] .dot{background:var(--part-line)} .chip[data-k=block] .dot{background:var(--block-line)}
.chip[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--ink);color:var(--ground);border-color:var(--ink)}
.chip:focus-visible,.toggle:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
kbd,code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85em;background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:5px;padding:.05rem .32rem}
.footnote{color:var(--faint);font-size:.82rem;margin-top:1rem;max-width:82ch}
.toggle{position:fixed;top:.8rem;right:.8rem;z-index:20;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.7rem;
  background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);border:1px solid var(--border-strong);border-radius:20px;
  padding:.35rem .7rem;cursor:pointer}
.hr{height:1px;background:var(--border);border:none;margin:3rem 0 0}
@media (max-width:560px){.band{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important}}
</style>

<button class="toggle" id="themeToggle" aria-label="Toggle colour theme">◐ theme</button>

<div class="wrap">
  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="eyebrow">Migration analysis · rev 11 · core/all tagged · post-merge</div>
    <h1>Replacing the Meltano taps with faucet-stream</h1>
    <p class="lede">All 47 <code>meltano_taps</code> sources → one BigQuery target, re-scored after the framework gaps merged to <code>main</code> (PRs #545 and #563) <strong>and every template was re-validated against the merged CLI</strong>. Each Supported tap now carries an honest scope tag: <span class="pill all">ALL</span> every stream the tap emits is reproduced, vs <span class="pill core">CORE</span> the primary streams are reproduced but a specific secondary stream/column still has a named gap.</p>
    <p class="meta"><b>What changed since rev 10:</b> the 12 migration-gap issues (#547–#558) + the tier-1 overwrite fan-out fix (#552) merged in <b>PR #563</b>. Templates upgraded to use them: <b>xero</b> journals keyset (#554), <b>salesforce</b> Bulk locator paging (#557), <b>attio</b> offset-in-body ×4 POST streams (#553), <b>stripe</b> event_id via record_ancestors (#549), <b>bamboohr</b> + <b>hibob</b> bulk/changed-tables via explode-with-parent-carry (#555); <b>hibob</b> labels stay DuckDB-free — inline via <code>humanReadable: APPEND</code> + a <code>named_lists</code> raw table for downstream joins. Child-fan-out into <code>overwrite</code> is now safe everywhere (#552). <b>The whole fleet uses inbuilt transforms only — zero <code>sql</code>/DuckDB transform in any template.</b> Also fixed 4 pre-existing template bugs the now-stricter <code>faucet validate</code> caught (acumatica explode, oracle_fusion/ukg_pro runtime-token-in-transform, syteline cast type/on_error). <b>Deploy state: 46 / 47 templates validate</b> (sage is the one blocked). <b>New gaps filed:</b> #567 (flow-capture→XML-body), #568 (set from a runtime token), #569 (ShopifyQL offset-into-string — #550 shipped variable-injection, which ShopifyQL can't use). <b>Rules:</b> _sdc_* dropped · inbuilt + SQL transforms count · WASM never · sink faucet-sink-bigquery · goal: same raw tables. <b>updated:</b> 2026-08-23</p>
  </header>

  <div class="band">
    <div class="stat ok"><div class="n">42<span class="delta">all streams</span></div><div class="l">Supported · ALL</div><div class="d">Every stream reproduced with stock connectors + <b>inbuilt transforms only — zero DuckDB/SQL transform in the entire fleet</b>. Validated (46/47 pass faucet validate).</div></div>
    <div class="stat core"><div class="n">3</div><div class="l">Supported · CORE</div><div class="d">Primary streams reproduced; one named secondary stream/column still gapped — ukg_pro, syteline, oracle_fusion.</div></div>
    <div class="stat part"><div class="n">1</div><div class="l">Partial</div><div class="d">shopify — orders/customers/products config-driven; the 2 ShopifyQL streams need offset-into-string paging (#569).</div></div>
    <div class="stat block"><div class="n">1</div><div class="l">Blocked</div><div class="d">sage — the captured Intacct sessionid can't be injected into the raw XML request body (#567); the template can't authenticate yet.</div></div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="callout note">
      <h3>How to read the scope tag — <span class="pill all">ALL</span> vs <span class="pill core">CORE</span></h3>
      <p><strong>ALL</strong> means the built template reproduces <em>every</em> stream the tap emits (primary + child + report + incremental), verified against the tap's real stream list and validated by <code>faucet validate</code>. <strong>CORE</strong> means the primary/entity streams are faithfully reproduced but a <em>specific</em> secondary stream or column is not yet — each CORE tap names exactly what and links the issue. This distinction is deliberate: "Supported" alone hid whether a tap's long tail was actually covered. Child-fan-out streams that write to an <code>overwrite</code> table are ALL-eligible only because <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/552">#552</a> (the tier-1 last-writer-wins fix) shipped — before it they silently kept only the last parent's rows.</p>
      <p><strong>The 3 CORE taps, precisely</strong> (bamboohr and hibob just moved to ALL — bamboohr's changed-tables and hibob's bulk-history streams are now wired with explode-with-parent-carry, #555; hibob stays DuckDB-free by getting labels inline via <code>humanReadable: APPEND</code> and emitting <code>named_lists</code> as a raw table for downstream joins): <strong>ukg_pro</strong> — every stream incl. the job×comp×employment cross-join is faithful; only <code>user_defined_field</code>'s parent <code>company_id</code> column can't be stamped (needs <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/568">#568</a>, filed — not merged; PK intact). <strong>syteline</strong> — IDO entity streams faithful; the report stored-procedures remain a caveat. <strong>oracle_fusion</strong> — the SOAP→XLSX report is faithful for one period per run; full history needs a per-period loop (<code>faucet backfill</code>). All three remaining framework gaps (<a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/568">#568</a> set-from-runtime-token, <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/567">#567</a> flow-capture→body, <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/569">#569</a> ShopifyQL offset-in-string) are filed but not yet merged.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="callout good">
      <h3>✓ The 12 gap issues + the tier-1 fix merged (PR #563), and the templates now use them</h3>
      <p><strong>#552</strong> (tier-1) — overwrite fan-out is begin-once/commit-once per destination, so a child stream fanned out over N parents into an <code>overwrite</code> table retains every parent's rows (was silent data loss). <strong>#547/#548</strong> resumable cursor + multi-array op-routing (plaid). <strong>#549</strong> record_ancestors (stripe event_id). <strong>#553</strong> offset/limit-in-body (attio POST-query). <strong>#554</strong> keyset/record-field cursor (xero journals). <strong>#557</strong> async-job result-set locator (salesforce Bulk). <strong>#550/#551</strong> graphql offset + zip_columns. <strong>#555</strong> explode parent-carry. <strong>#556</strong> oauth2_refresh scope + rotation (onedrive/rippling). <strong>#558</strong> reference table from a live API.</p>
      <p><strong>Honest correction found while re-verifying:</strong> #550 as merged injects the offset as a GraphQL <em>variable</em>, but ShopifyQL needs the offset <em>inside the query string</em> (<code>LIMIT n OFFSET n</code>) — a variable can't interpolate into a GraphQL string literal. So shopify's <code>sessions</code>/<code>sales</code> are still gapped; filed as <a href="https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/569">#569</a>. Better to catch it here than ship a template that silently pages nothing.</p>
